 ],
 "text": "Uber just gave AI to 30,000 staff. The tool wasn't the trick. The rollout was, and you can copy it. Step 1, start small. Uber ran a pilot with about 1,000 people, and 8 in 10 of them weren't engineers. So don't hand AI to your tech person. Hand it to ops. Step 2, sit next to each team for 2 weeks. Uber paired 30 AI engineers with teams to find the boring work. Step 3, automate that first. Data reports, training in new languages, dashboards. Then scale. Buying licenses and sending a login isn't a rollout. It's how we roll out AI at Content Systems.ai. Bring your biggest bottleneck to our free office hours. Link in bio."
